      "message": "Possible SQL injection",
      "note": "False positive: `SET` accepts no bind parameters, so the timeout has to be interpolated. The value is never request-derived -- it comes from ZIMMER_CONTENT_SEARCH_BUDGET_SECONDS (an operator-set env var) or the DEFAULT_TIME_BUDGET_SECONDS literal -- and it is forced through Integer() and clamped to 1..120000 before it reaches the string, so the interpolated text is always a bare integer. Everything a caller supplies (the query, the cursor, the id list) reaches Postgres as a bind parameter.",
